WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.162 --> 00:00:10.163
One day a young bird was learning to fly.

2
00:00:10.183 --> 00:00:13.123
"Whee! This is fun!"

3
00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:15.564
he said, flapping his wings.

4
00:00:16.544 --> 00:00:19.125
Suddenly another bird flew by.

5
00:00:19.145 --> 00:00:23.786
"Wow! What kind of bird was that?"

6
00:00:24.186 --> 00:00:24.887
he wondered.

7
00:00:24.907 --> 00:00:26.807
"How cool!"

8
00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:29.768
He decided to follow the other bird.

9
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.462
On his way he met a squirrel.

10
00:00:33.482 --> 00:00:39.446
"Hey, Squirrel," he said, "did you see a bird go by?"

11
00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.867
The squirrel was confused.

12
00:00:42.568 --> 00:00:43.208
"What bird?"

13
00:00:43.568 --> 00:00:44.069
he said.

14
00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:48.292
"Just a moment ago, a bird flew by us.

15
00:00:48.612 --> 00:00:49.652
Didn't you see it?"

16
00:00:50.013 --> 00:00:51.213
the bird asked again.

17
00:00:51.954 --> 00:00:53.315
The squirrel smiled.

18
00:00:53.335 --> 00:00:55.716
"Oh, that was not a bird.

19
00:00:55.937 --> 00:00:56.637
That was me!"

20
00:00:56.657 --> 00:01:00.760
"You?" said the bird.

21
00:01:02.008 --> 00:01:03.609
"But you are a squirrel!

22
00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:05.729
Squirrels cannot fly!"

23
00:01:05.749 --> 00:01:09.810
"Well, I can," said the squirrel.

24
00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.631
"I am a flying squirrel!

25
00:01:11.951 --> 00:01:12.511
Watch me!"

26
00:01:13.831 --> 00:01:16.032
The squirrel jumped off the branch.

27
00:01:16.572 --> 00:01:20.633
He stretched his arms and legs, and soared through the air.

28
00:01:20.653 --> 00:01:23.934
"Oh, that was awesome!"

29
00:01:24.374 --> 00:01:25.654
the little bird said.

30
00:01:25.674 --> 00:01:29.415
"But your wings do not look like my wings."

31
00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:33.293
"No," explained the flying squirrel.

32
00:01:33.313 --> 00:01:34.914
"I do not have wings.

33
00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:37.216
I have flaps of skin on my sides.

34
00:01:37.636 --> 00:01:40.658
I stretch these flaps and I can glide for a long time.

35
00:01:41.058 --> 00:01:43.119
Now you know flying is not just for birds!"

36
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.762
Just then an insect flew by.

37
00:01:47.782 --> 00:01:51.504
"Oh, my favorite kind of insect!"

38
00:01:51.964 --> 00:01:52.725
said the bird.

39
00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.747
"Oh, that is my favorite too!"

40
00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:57.368
the squirrel agreed.

41
00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:02.263
The squirrel and the bird followed the insect to the stream.

42
00:02:03.724 --> 00:02:07.907
Suddenly a fish flew out of the water and glided by them.

43
00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.428
"What was that?

44
00:02:09.808 --> 00:02:10.408
Did you see it?"

45
00:02:10.809 --> 00:02:11.669
asked the squirrel.

46
00:02:11.689 --> 00:02:14.811
"I cannot believe what I saw!"

47
00:02:15.332 --> 00:02:16.092
said the bird.

48
00:02:16.112 --> 00:02:18.234
"Fish cannot fly!"

49
00:02:19.695 --> 00:02:21.376
The fish swam up to them.

50
00:02:21.396 --> 00:02:22.977
"You are right!"

51
00:02:23.297 --> 00:02:24.198
the fish said.

52
00:02:24.218 --> 00:02:25.519
"But I can.

53
00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:26.900
I am a flying fish.

54
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.961
I can glide through the air when a bigger fish tries to eat me.

55
00:02:32.261 --> 00:02:33.041
I have to go now.

56
00:02:33.381 --> 00:02:36.622
Bye!" And the fish swam away.

57
00:02:36.642 --> 00:02:42.624
"Gee! I have never seen a fish fly before," said the bird.

58
00:02:42.644 --> 00:02:45.965
"Well, Squirrel, you were right!

59
00:02:46.325 --> 00:02:49.125
I guess flying really isn't just for birds."

60
00:02:49.145 --> 00:02:52.947
"Good-bye, Bird," said the squirrel.

61
00:02:52.967 --> 00:02:56.047
"I have to tell my family about the flying fish!"

62
00:02:56.447 --> 00:02:58.108
He leaped into the air.

63
00:02:59.084 --> 00:03:01.106
"Good-bye!" said the bird.

64
00:03:01.126 --> 00:03:04.068
"I have to tell my mom about this.

65
00:03:04.789 --> 00:03:07.051
You never know what might fly by!"
